%% The generated router, drawn in the order it actually asks its questions.
%% The mistake this diagram exists to prevent is the belief that a method is
%% selected by its name. Three things select it, in this order: whether the
%% call carries arguments at all, whether its OnComplete is one the method
%% allows, and only then the four bytes in argument zero. The application-ID
%% check is a separate question asked afterwards -- which is why a method that
%% opts out of it with create=allow is matched before the question is put.
%% .
%% Two diamonds only, and the OnComplete filter is a rectangle: a Mermaid
%% diamond holding three lines of text is roughly three times the height of a
%% rectangle holding the same text, and this figure has to fit on one page.
%% Flowchart rather than stateDiagram-v2, and no subgraphs: a subgraph's own
%% direction is ignored once edges cross its boundary.
flowchart TB
    T["An application call arrives<br/>app ID · OnComplete · argument array"]
    A{"Any application<br/>arguments?"}
    B["Bare route · no selector to match<br/>the OnComplete alone picks the method,<br/>at most one per action, and it runs"]
    C["The OnComplete must be one the method allows<br/>NoOp · OptIn · CloseOut · Update · Delete"]
    D["Methods declaring create=allow are matched<br/>on argument zero here, with no ID check"]
    E{"Is the application<br/>ID zero?"}
    F["create=require<br/>creation methods"]
    G["create=disallow, the default<br/>ordinary methods"]
    H["The method body runs"]
    X["err · nothing matched<br/>the call is rejected"]

    T --> A
    A -->|"no"| B
    A -->|"yes"| C
    C --> D
    D -->|"matched"| H
    D -->|"no match yet"| E
    E -->|"zero · a creation"| F
    E -->|"non-zero · it exists"| G
    F -->|"matched"| H
    G -->|"matched"| H
    F -->|"no match"| X
    G -->|"no match"| X

    classDef step fill:#f2f2f2,stroke:#333333,color:#111111
    classDef ask fill:#ffffff,stroke:#333333,color:#111111
    classDef bad fill:#e0e0e0,stroke:#333333,color:#111111
    class T,B,C,F,G,H step
    class A,E ask
    class D,X bad
